\fs32\b Troubleshooting\b0\fs20\par
\par
This section gives some simple checks to make if WinBMD2 does not behave as expected.\par
\par
\fs24\b The expected scan is not displayed\b0\fs20\par
Check that the batch information on the Header Form is correct, particularly the year, quarter, page and source information.\par
\par
If automatic scan display is turned off in Options, use the Scan commands to display the scan manually.\par
\par
See the Scans topic and its Finding Scans section for more information.\par
\par
\fs24\b The scan cannot be found\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 needs sufficient information to identify the required scan. Check the information on the Header Form and correct it using Edit Header if necessary.\par
\par
A scan may also be temporarily unavailable from its online source. If necessary, try again later.\par
\par
\fs24\b A transcription cannot be uploaded\b0\fs20\par
Before uploading, make sure that the transcription is complete and that every required row has been verified.\par
\par
A tick mark should appear at the end of each verified row in the grid.\par
\par
Also check that the Current FreeBMD User ID and Password on the Header Form are correct.\par
\par
If WinBMD2 reports an error during upload, read the message carefully as it may identify the problem which needs to be corrected.\par
\par
\fs24\b A value is rejected or a warning is displayed\b0\fs20\par
WinBMD2 checks many entries while they are being transcribed. A warning means that the value appears unusual or does not have the expected format.\par
\par
Always check the original scan. If the unusual value really is what appears in the index, it may still be the correct value to transcribe.\par
\par
\fs24\b The windows are in an inconvenient position\b0\fs20\par
The WinBMD2 windows can be resized and moved independently. Their positions and sizes are remembered for future sessions.\par
\par
This is particularly useful when the transcription grid and ScanView are being used on separate monitors.\par
\par
\fs24\b Something still does not work\b0\fs20\par
If the problem continues, make a note of what you were doing when it occurred and any error message displayed by WinBMD2.\par
\par
This information can be useful when asking for assistance.\par
